"A namespace package is a package that only contains other packages and "
"modules, with no direct contents of its own.  Such packages can be split "
"across multiple, separately-packaged distributions.  They are normally used "
"to split up large packages produced by a single organization, such as in the "
"``zope`` namespace package for Zope Corporation packages, and the ``peak`` "
"namespace package for the Python Enterprise Application Kit."
