msgid "0.6b1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1759
msgid ""
"Split ``get_platform()`` into ``get_supported_platform()`` and "
"``get_build_platform()`` to work around a Mac versioning problem that caused "
"the behavior of ``compatible_platforms()`` to be platform specific."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1763
msgid ""
"Fix entry point parsing when a standalone module name has whitespace between "
"it and the extras."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1766
msgid "0.6a11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1767
msgid ""
"Added ``ExtractionError`` and ``ResourceManager.extraction_error()`` so that "
"cache permission problems get a more user-friendly explanation of the "
"problem, and so that programs can catch and handle extraction errors if they "
"need to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1772
msgid "0.6a10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1773
msgid ""
"Added the ``extras`` attribute to ``Distribution``, the ``find_plugins()`` "
"method to ``WorkingSet``, and the ``__add__()`` and ``__iadd__()`` methods "
"to ``Environment``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1777
msgid "``safe_name()`` now allows dots in project names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1779
msgid ""
"There is a new ``to_filename()`` function that escapes project names and "
"versions for safe use in constructing egg filenames from a Distribution "
"object's metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1783
msgid ""
"Added ``Distribution.clone()`` method, and keyword argument support to other "
"``Distribution`` constructors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1786
msgid ""
"Added the ``DEVELOP_DIST`` precedence, and automatically assign it to eggs "
"using ``.egg-info`` format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1789
msgid "0.6a9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1790
msgid ""
"Don't raise an error when an invalid (unfinished) distribution is found "
"unless absolutely necessary.  Warn about skipping invalid/unfinished eggs "
"when building an Environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1794
msgid ""
"Added support for ``.egg-info`` files or directories with version/platform "
"information embedded in the filename, so that system packagers have the "
"option of including ``PKG-INFO`` files to indicate the presence of a system-"
"installed egg, without needing to use ``.egg`` directories, zipfiles, or ``."
"pth`` manipulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1800
msgid ""
"Changed ``parse_version()`` to remove dashes before pre-release tags, so "
"that ``0.2-rc1`` is considered an *older* version than ``0.2``, and is equal "
"to ``0.2rc1``.  The idea that a dash *always* meant a post-release version "
"was highly non-intuitive to setuptools users and Python developers, who seem "
"to want to use ``-rc`` version numbers a lot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1806
msgid "0.6a8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1807
msgid ""
"Fixed a problem with ``WorkingSet.resolve()`` that prevented version "
"conflicts from being detected at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1810
msgid ""
"Improved runtime conflict warning message to identify a line in the user's "
"program, rather than flagging the ``warn()`` call in ``pkg_resources``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1813
msgid ""
"Avoid giving runtime conflict warnings for namespace packages, even if they "
"were declared by a different package than the one currently being activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1816
msgid "Fix path insertion algorithm for case-insensitive filesystems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1818
msgid ""
"Fixed a problem with nested namespace packages (e.g. ``peak.util``) not "
"being set as an attribute of their parent package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1821
msgid "0.6a6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1822
msgid ""
"Activated distributions are now inserted in ``sys.path`` (and the working "
"set) just before the directory that contains them, instead of at the end. "
"This allows e.g. eggs in ``site-packages`` to override unmanaged modules in "
"the same location, and allows eggs found earlier on ``sys.path`` to override "
"ones found later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1828
msgid ""
"When a distribution is activated, it now checks whether any contained non-"
"namespace modules have already been imported and issues a warning if a "
"conflicting module has already been imported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1832
msgid ""
"Changed dependency processing so that it's breadth-first, allowing a "
"depender's preferences to override those of a dependee, to prevent conflicts "
"when a lower version is acceptable to the dependee, but not the depender."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1836
msgid ""
"Fixed a problem extracting zipped files on Windows, when the egg in question "
"has had changed contents but still has the same version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1839
msgid "0.6a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1840
msgid "Fix a bug in ``WorkingSet.resolve()`` that was introduced in 0.6a3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1842
msgid "0.6a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1843
msgid ""
"Added ``safe_extra()`` parsing utility routine, and use it for Requirement, "
"EntryPoint, and Distribution objects' extras handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1846
msgid "0.6a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1847
msgid ""
"Enhanced performance of ``require()`` and related operations when all "
"requirements are already in the working set, and enhanced performance of "
"directory scanning for distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1851
msgid ""
"Fixed some problems using ``pkg_resources`` w/PEP 302 loaders other than "
"``zipimport``, and the previously-broken \"eager resource\" support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1854
msgid ""
"Fixed ``pkg_resources.resource_exists()`` not working correctly, along with "
"some other resource API bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1857
msgid "Many API changes and enhancements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1859
msgid ""
"Added ``EntryPoint``, ``get_entry_map``, ``load_entry_point``, and "
"``get_entry_info`` APIs for dynamic plugin discovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1862
msgid "``list_resources`` is now ``resource_listdir`` (and it actually works)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1864
msgid ""
"Resource API functions like ``resource_string()`` that accepted a package "
"name and resource name, will now also accept a ``Requirement`` object in "
"place of the package name (to allow access to non-package data files in an "
"egg)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1869
msgid ""
"``get_provider()`` will now accept a ``Requirement`` instance or a module "
"name.  If it is given a ``Requirement``, it will return a corresponding "
"``Distribution`` (by calling ``require()`` if a suitable distribution isn't "
"already in the working set), rather than returning a metadata and resource "
"provider for a specific module.  (The difference is in how resource paths "
"are interpreted; supplying a module name means resources path will be module-"
"relative, rather than relative to the distribution's root.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1878
msgid ""
"``Distribution`` objects now implement the ``IResourceProvider`` and "
"``IMetadataProvider`` interfaces, so you don't need to reference the (no "
"longer available) ``metadata`` attribute to get at these interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1882
msgid ""
"``Distribution`` and ``Requirement`` both have a ``project_name`` attribute "
"for the project name they refer to.  (Previously these were ``name`` and "
"``distname`` attributes.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1886
msgid ""
"The ``path`` attribute of ``Distribution`` objects is now ``location``, "
"because it isn't necessarily a filesystem path (and hasn't been for some "
"time now).  The ``location`` of ``Distribution`` objects in the filesystem "
"should always be normalized using ``pkg_resources.normalize_path()``; all of "
"the setuptools' code that generates distributions from the filesystem "
"(including ``Distribution.from_filename()``) ensure this invariant, but if "
"you use a more generic API like ``Distribution()`` or ``Distribution."
"from_location()`` you should take care that you don't create a distribution "
"with an un-normalized filesystem path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1896
msgid ""
"``Distribution`` objects now have an ``as_requirement()`` method that "
"returns a ``Requirement`` for the distribution's project name and version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1899
msgid ""
"Distribution objects no longer have an ``installed_on()`` method, and the "
"``install_on()`` method is now ``activate()`` (but may go away altogether "
"soon).  The ``depends()`` method has also been renamed to ``requires()``, "
"and ``InvalidOption`` is now ``UnknownExtra``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1904
msgid ""
"``find_distributions()`` now takes an additional argument called ``only``, "
"that tells it to only yield distributions whose location is the passed-in "
"path.  (It defaults to False, so that the default behavior is unchanged.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1908
msgid ""
"``AvailableDistributions`` is now called ``Environment``, and the ``get()``, "
"``__len__()``, and ``__contains__()`` methods were removed, because they "
"weren't particularly useful.  ``__getitem__()`` no longer raises "
"``KeyError``; it just returns an empty list if there are no distributions "
"for the named project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1914
msgid ""
"The ``resolve()`` method of ``Environment`` is now a method of "
"``WorkingSet`` instead, and the ``best_match()`` method now uses a working "
"set instead of a path list as its second argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1918
msgid ""
"There is a new ``pkg_resources.add_activation_listener()`` API that lets you "
"register a callback for notifications about distributions added to ``sys."
"path`` (including the distributions already on it).  This is basically a "
"hook for extensible applications and frameworks to be able to search for "
"plugin metadata in distributions added at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1924
msgid "0.5a13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1925
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug in resource extraction from nested packages in a zipped egg."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1927
msgid "0.5a12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1928
msgid ""
"Updated extraction/cache mechanism for zipped resources to avoid inter-"
"process and inter-thread races during extraction.  The default cache "
"location can now be set via the ``PYTHON_EGGS_CACHE`` environment variable, "
"and the default Windows cache is now a ``Python-Eggs`` subdirectory of the "
"current user's \"Application Data\" directory, if the ``PYTHON_EGGS_CACHE`` "
"variable isn't set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1935
msgid "0.5a10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1936
msgid ""
"Fix a problem with ``pkg_resources`` being confused by non-existent eggs on "
"``sys.path`` (e.g. if a user deletes an egg without removing it from the "
"``easy-install.pth`` file)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1940
msgid ""
"Fix a problem with \"basket\" support in ``pkg_resources``, where egg-"
"finding never actually went inside ``.egg`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1943
msgid ""
"Made ``pkg_resources`` import the module you request resources from, if it's "
"not already imported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1946
msgid "0.5a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1947
msgid ""
"``pkg_resources.AvailableDistributions.resolve()`` and related methods now "
"accept an ``installer`` argument: a callable taking one argument, a "
"``Requirement`` instance.  The callable must return a ``Distribution`` "
"object, or ``None`` if no distribution is found.  This feature is used by "
"EasyInstall to resolve dependencies by recursively invoking itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1953
msgid "0.4a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1954
msgid ""
"Fix problems with ``resource_listdir()``, ``resource_isdir()`` and resource "
"directory extraction for zipped eggs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1957
msgid "0.4a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1958
msgid ""
"Fixed scripts not being able to see a ``__file__`` variable in ``__main__``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1960
msgid ""
"Fixed a problem with ``resource_isdir()`` implementation that was introduced "
"in 0.4a2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1963
msgid "0.4a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1964
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug in requirements processing for exact versions (i.e. ``==`` and "
"``!=``) when only one condition was included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1967
msgid ""
"Added ``safe_name()`` and ``safe_version()`` APIs to clean up handling of "
"arbitrary distribution names and versions found on PyPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1970
msgid "0.3a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1971
msgid ""
"``pkg_resources`` now supports resource directories, not just the resources "
"in them.  In particular, there are ``resource_listdir()`` and "
"``resource_isdir()`` APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1975
msgid ""
"``pkg_resources`` now supports \"egg baskets\" -- .egg zipfiles which "
"contain multiple distributions in subdirectories whose names end with ``."
"egg``. Having such a \"basket\" in a directory on ``sys.path`` is equivalent "
"to having the individual eggs in that directory, but the contained eggs can "
"be individually added (or not) to ``sys.path``.  Currently, however, there "
"is no automated way to create baskets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/pkg_resources.rst:1982
msgid ""
"Namespace package manipulation is now protected by the Python import lock."
msgstr ""

